      "FLAT.1": "The patient's ECG shows irregularly irregular tachycardia with grouped beating and intermittently visible P waves, which is consistent with Orthodromic Atrioventricular Reentrant Tachycardia (ORT). The ECG after diltiazem administration shows regular narrow complex tachycardia with visible P waves, and the cycle length between visible P waves is 440 milliseconds, which further supports the diagnosis of ORT. Additionally, the patient's response to adenosine administration, which shows temporary heart block with continuation of supraventricular tachycardia, is also consistent with ORT."
    }
